{"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftNLP\/documentation\/SwiftNLP"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WordNet"},{"text":" is a large lexical database of English where nouns, verbs, adjectives, and adverbs are organized into sets of cognitive synonyms called ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Synsets"}]},{"text":", interlinked by conceptual-semantic and lexical relations.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"1-Looking-Up-Synsets--Definitions","text":"1. Looking Up Synsets & Definitions"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import SwiftNLP","","let wordnet = WordNet.shared","","\/\/ Look up all noun synsets for \"bank\"","let synsets = wordnet.synsets(for: \"bank\", pos: .noun)","for s in synsets {","    print(\"ID: \\(s.id), Definition: \\(s.definition)\")","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"2-Semantic-Similarity-Metrics","text":"2. Semantic Similarity Metrics"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"SwiftSci implements standard lexical similarity algorithms:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Path Similarity"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Shortest path distance in the hypernym taxonomy:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Formula:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sim_path(s1, s2) = 1 \/ (1 + distance(s1, s2))"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Note"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Wu-Palmer Similarity (WUP)"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Measures depth of least common subsumer (LCS) relative to synset depths:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"aside","s